// TEMPLATE: copy a block into a file of your pack, remove the "// " in front of
// each line, give it a new ID and fill in the fields. Everything here is
// commented out, so this file adds nothing to the game.
//
// IDs use lowercase letters, digits and underscores, and never change once
// released (saves refer to them). Indent with four spaces.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- location
// == location my_place
// name: My Place
// region: my_region
// zone: my_zone                (or "none": nothing to find by exploring)
// map: 3, 4                    (column, row on the region's map grid)
// flags: fast travel           (also: safe rest, known at start)
// items: some_item             (items lying here)
// exits:
//     north: other_place
// description:
//     What the player sees. [if time is night]At night.[else]By day.[end if]
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- character
// == character my_person
// name: Sam
// pronouns: they
// lives at: my_place
// values:
//     trust: wary, friendly, close
//     met: flag
// talk:
//     Sam waves. 'Hello there.'
//     -> my_person.talk
//
// == menu my_person.talk
// title: What do you want to talk about?
// leave: Goodbye
// * A topic -- A short description [if not my_person.met]
//     'Nice to meet you,' Sam says.
//     ~ my_person.met = yes
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- quest
// == quest my_quest
// name: A small favour
// stages:
//     not_started
//     asked: Sam asked you for help.
//     done: You helped Sam.
// done at: done
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- item
// == item my_item
// name: shiny pebble
// description: A smooth, shiny pebble.
// weight: 1
// category: other              (food, drink, medical, clothing, weapon, collectible, other)
// use:
//     You turn the pebble over in your hand.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- event
// == event my_event
// name: Something odd
// found by: exploring in my_zone
// repeat: until resolved
// play:
//     Something odd happens.
//     * Look closer
//         ~ give my_item
//         ~ resolve
//     * Walk away
//         You walk away.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- scene
// == scene my_scene
// Plain lines are text. Lines starting with ~ are effects:
// ~ player.hunger - 10
// "-> other_scene" goes to another scene, "play other_scene" plays it and comes back.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- creature and form
// == creature my_creature
// name: Wild Thing
// found in: my_zone
// level: 1
// hp: 12
// damage: 3
// form: my_creature
// gender: male
// encounter:
//     A wild thing appears!
// attack:
//     [one of]It swipes at you![or]It lunges![at random]
// defeated:
//     It runs away.
// victory:
//     It wins, and you feel strange.
//
// == form my_creature
// name: Wild Thing
// tail:
//     description: A short, wild tail.
//     change: a short tail sprouts behind you
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- door
// == door my_door
// name: Garden gate
// locked: not player has gate_key   (yes, no, or a condition)
// locked text: The gate is locked.
// shown in room: A garden gate leads north.
// (use it in both places' exits:  north: other_place, door my_door)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- arrival / leaving event
// == event my_arrival
// name: A welcome
// found by: arriving at my_place      (or: walking into, travelling to, leaving my_place north)
// repeat: once
// chance: 50%
// cooldown: 4                          (turns before it can come up again)
// requires: time is night
// play:
//     A cat greets you at the door.
//     ~ continue moving                (leaving events only: the player walks on)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- values for the whole pack
// == values my_pack
// values:
//     coins_found: number
//     visited_tower: flag
//     mood: calm, nervous, scared       (states, in order)
//     last_visit: time                  (for "since my_pack.last_visit > 2 turns")
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- text snippet
// == text my_snippet
// [one of]It is quiet.[or]Wind moves the leaves.[at random]
// (use it in any text as [my_snippet])
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- condition (timed state)
// == condition my_condition
// name: Energized
// shows: Str +1.
// while active:
//     player.strength + 1
// ends:
//     The energy wears off.
// (start it with:  ~ condition my_condition for 6 hours)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- meter
// == meter my_meter
// name: Tiredness
// value: player.tiredness
// decay: 1
// limit: 10
// stages:
//     5: my_condition
// at limit:
//     You collapse.
// (change it with:  ~ meter my_meter + 2)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- hook
// == hook my_hook
// on: each turn
// when: time is night and chance 1 in 4
// do:
//     An owl hoots somewhere.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- captivity
// == captivity my_trap
// name: Stuck in the mud
// escape at: 3
// status: Pulls: [captivity.struggle] of 3
// struggle label: Pull
// start:
//     Your boots sink into the mud.
// situation:
//     The mud holds you fast.
// struggle:
//     You pull hard.
// escape:
//     With a sucking sound, you come free.
// (start it from a scene with:  play my_trap)
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- creature variants
// == creature my_creature
// ...
// variants:
//     female:
//         gender: female
//     male:
//         gender: male
//         hp: 16
// (scenes test "my_creature is variant male"; fights can name one: "fight my_creature (male):")
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- filter, tag, level, feat
// == filter my_filter
// name: Spiders
// description: Spider creatures.
//
// == tag my_tag
// name: Insects
//
// == level my_level
// name: Scenery
// default: standard
// options:
//     less: Short.
//     standard: Normal.
//     more: Long.
// (test it with:  level my_level is more)
//
// == feat my_feat
// name: Lucky
// description: You find more while exploring.
// exploration bonus: 2
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- scenario
// == scenario my_start
// name: A new beginning
// start: my_place
// description: Shown on the New game screen.
// setup:
//     ~ give my_item quietly
// intro:
//     The opening text.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- scavenging rules
// == scavenge_rules my_scavenging
// generic: my_generic_find            (an event found by scavenging)
// generic chance: 2 in 3
// target: 8
// start: You search around.
// found: You come across
// failure: You find nothing.
// only at: You can only scavenge at fast travel points.

